{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero divisor zero divisor","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","fileName":"Zero Divisor.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Divisor","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]] · [[Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Integral Domain","Nilpotent Element","Zero Divisor on a Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero divisor zero divisor","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","fileName":"Zero Divisor.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Divisor","heading":"Zero Divisor","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A zero divisor is a nonzero element a of a ring for which another nonzero element c satisfies ac = 0. Zero divisors cannot occur in an [[Integral Domain]].\n\nEvery nonzero [[Nilpotent Element]] is a zero divisor because some lower positive power is nonzero while its product with a further power is zero. Zero divisors also motivate the module-specific notion of a [[Zero Divisor on a Module]].\n\nThe book uses zero divisors as the dividing line between general commutative rings and [[Integral Domain|integral domains]]. Their absence makes multiplicative cancellation valid and is essential when degrees of nonzero polynomial products are added.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Integral Domain","Nilpotent Element","Zero Divisor on a Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"zero divisor zero divisor","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Zero Divisor.md","fileName":"Zero Divisor.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Zero Divisor","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Integral Domain","Nilpotent Element","Zero Divisor on a Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}